Premier League Overview Page
Overview & Purpose
Provides a macro-level statistical summary of the Premier League season, focusing on league-wide age demographics, goal generation versus expected goals (xG), age group appearances, top performers, and national contributions.

Key Insights
League Scale: Evaluated 1,116 players across the league with an average age profile of 25 years, generating 1,115 total goals and 340K total passes.

Age Group Dominance: Players in their Prime age category account for the highest concentration of total goals, xG, and overall appearances, outperforming Experienced and Veteran categories.

xG Realization: Goal production aligns tightly with expected goals (xG) metrics across age categories, indicating strong finish efficiency league-wide.

Top Attacking Outlets: Mohamed Salah leads the league in total Goal Actions (G/A), followed by Alexander Isak, Bryan Mbeumo, Erling Haaland, and Ollie Watkins.

Nationality Impact: English players drive the majority of total Goal Actions (60.96% / 534 G/A), followed by players from Brazil (14.84% / 130 G/A) and Portugal (9.25% / 81 G/A).
